# Drift events: each violates the java-service SBoB (slot 3) and MUST fire the
# mapped rule. These are the Java2Shell (CVE-2026-114938) post-RCE behaviors:
# the point of the scenario is that the SBoB catches the BEHAVIOR after the
# JIT-level RCE lands, regardless of the entry vector.
#
#   execve /bin/sh -c ...                -> 100311 (SBoB drift: process ...)
#        post-RCE shell spawn from the JVM — execs[] declares only the JVM
#   open /var/www/webapp/shell.jsp       -> 100321 (SBoB drift: file open ...)
#        the dropped JSP webshell — /var/www/webapp is not in opens[] (the
#        only declared write path is /var/lib/app-data/*)
#   connect 127.0.0.1:4445 (C2 stand-in) -> 100331 (SBoB drift: connect ...)
#        the C2 callback — egress[] declares only 10.96.100.30:8443
#
# The fourth post-RCE behavior — defineClass staging fully in-JVM — is
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT from this corpus: it performs no exec, no undeclared
# open and no connect, so it is expected-silent (the committed finding in
# docs/java2shell/detection-evidence.md). The moment the payload touches the
# OS (exec, file, socket), drift fires.

